<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Proof of
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>:
From affine estimates to the half-turn bound</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following proposition controls the part of the <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>-spectrum near
<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.5</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Interpolation bound on the <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>-spectral subspace
associated with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\frac{1}{2},1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\frac{1}{2},1]</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq c</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[1/2,1]}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ran</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[1/2,1]}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w\|^{2}\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}w\|\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{3}w\|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w\|^{2}\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}w\|\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{3}w\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We regard <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> as operators on
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math> and work with the spectral subspaces</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}\coloneqq\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[1/2,1]}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathcal{H}^{\prime}\coloneqq\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[-1/2,1/2)}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mi>ran</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mi>ran</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}\coloneqq\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[1/2,1]}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathcal{H}^{\prime}\coloneqq\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[-1/2,1/2)}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}=\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition C.5 (Interpolation bound on the 𝖴_𝖯𝖯-spectral subspace associated with [1/2,1]). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a> yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}v\|^{2}\leq C\,\|v\|\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}v\|\,\hskip 20.00003pt\forall v\in\mathcal{H}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.317em;" width="2.317em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}v\|^{2}\leq C\,\|v\|\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}v\|\,\hskip 20.00003pt\forall v\in\mathcal{H}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that by <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>,
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\rm gap}^{2}I\preceq\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}\preceq I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\rm gap}^{2}I\preceq\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4 (Comparison of positive operators). ‣ D.3 Comparison of positive operators ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a> with <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{A}=C^{-1/2}\,(\mathsf{T}^{*}\mathsf{T})^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝖳</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>𝖳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}=C^{-1/2}\,(\mathsf{T}^{*}\mathsf{T})^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}|_{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}|_{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\gamma_{\rm gap}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\gamma_{\rm gap}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=1</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}\coloneqq(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}|_{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}\coloneqq(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}|_{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, gives a factor
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})</annotation></semantics></math>, up to a universal constant. Shrinking the
universal constant <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> in the assumption if necessary, we may suppose that
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1/16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1/16</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\rm gap}\leq 2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\rm gap}\leq 2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, so the additive constant is
absorbed by <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}\,\hskip 20.00003pt\forall v\in\mathcal{H}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.317em;" width="2.317em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}v\|^{2}\,\hskip 20.00003pt\forall v\in\mathcal{H}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, on <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, no further spectral localization
is needed. Since <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> is a contraction,
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isometry, and
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}\succeq\frac{3}{4}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}\succeq\frac{3}{4}I</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\|\leq 2\,\|v\|\leq 4\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}v\|\,\hskip 20.00003pt\forall v\in\mathcal{H}^{\prime}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.317em;" width="2.317em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}v\|\leq 2\,\|v\|\leq 4\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}v\|\,\hskip 20.00003pt\forall v\in\mathcal{H}^{\prime}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">For a general <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>, decompose
<math id="A3.SS3.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=v_{\mathcal{H}}+v_{\mathcal{H}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=v_{\mathcal{H}}+v_{\mathcal{H}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining the preceding two
estimates with <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a+b)^{2}\leq 2a^{2}+2b^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a+b)^{2}\leq 2a^{2}+2b^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and using that <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>
commutes with <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, proves
(<a href="#A2.E17" title="Equation B.17 ‣ Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.17</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We prove <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition C.5 (Interpolation bound on the 𝖴_𝖯𝖯-spectral subspace associated with [1/2,1]). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a> after the following preparatory results. The first
approximates <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w</annotation></semantics></math>, conditionally on <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, by a function
that is affine in the rescaled coordinate <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=(X-Y_{+})/\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=(X-Y_{+})/\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, so
that <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition C.2 (Weighted half-turn estimate for affine functions). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> applies. The second bounds the resulting
affine data by the gradients of <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w</annotation></semantics></math>, using the
derivative formula (<a href="#A3.E8" title="Equation C.8 ‣ Lemma C.1 (Derivative formula for 𝖴_𝖯𝖯). ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>). Both results hold
for arbitrary functions in <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math>; the spectral
condition enters when we invert <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Recall from <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> the conditional law
<math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}\coloneqq\Law(W\mid Y_{+}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}\coloneqq\Law(W\mid Y_{+}=y)</annotation></semantics></math>, its mean <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{w}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance
<math id="A3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and that, conditionally on <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}=y</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=y+\sqrt{\eta}\,W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=y+\sqrt{\eta}\,W</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{-}=y+2\sqrt{\eta}\,W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{-}=y+2\sqrt{\eta}\,W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.6</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conditional affine approximation and energy bound)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math>, and let
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{y}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[\nabla w(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{y}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[\nabla w(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the conditional mean of
the gradient. For <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>-almost every <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y}(u)\coloneqq w(y+2\sqrt{\eta}u)-(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}w)(y)-2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}^{\top}(u-\bar{w}_{y})\,,\hskip 20.00003ptu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y}(u)\coloneqq w(y+2\sqrt{\eta}u)-(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}w)(y)-2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}^{\top}(u-\bar{w}_{y})\,,\hskip 20.00003ptu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>-mean zero, the decomposition</span></p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w=2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{Y_{+}}^{\top}(W-\bar{w}_{Y_{+}})+e_{Y_{+}}(W)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w=2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{Y_{+}}^{\top}(W-\bar{w}_{Y_{+}})+e_{Y_{+}}(W)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">holds in <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>, and, with</span></p>
<table id="A3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}\coloneqq\|\nabla w\|^{2}-\int\|a_{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)=\mathbb{E}\|\nabla w(Y_{-})-a_{Y_{+}}\|^{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}\coloneqq\|\nabla w\|^{2}-\int\|a_{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)=\mathbb{E}\|\nabla w(Y_{-})-a_{Y_{+}}\|^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">one has</span></p>
<table id="A3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[e_{Y_{+}}(W)^{2}]\leq 4\eta\mathcal{R}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[e_{Y_{+}}(W)^{2}]\leq 4\eta\mathcal{R}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, if <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq c</annotation></semantics></math> for a sufficiently small
universal constant <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}+\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq C\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.039em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.039em">∥</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}+\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq C\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w=w(Y_{-})-\mathbb{E}[w(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}]=w(Y_{-})-(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}w)(Y_{+})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w=w(Y_{-})-\mathbb{E}[w(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}]=w(Y_{-})-(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}w)(Y_{+})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Conditioning on <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}=y</annotation></semantics></math> and substituting <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{-}=y+2\sqrt{\eta}\,W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{-}=y+2\sqrt{\eta}\,W</annotation></semantics></math>
gives, for <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>-almost every <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w)(u)=w(y+2\sqrt{\eta}u)-(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}w)(y)\,,\hskip 20.00003ptu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w)(u)=w(y+2\sqrt{\eta}u)-(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}w)(y)\,,\hskip 20.00003ptu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is (<a href="#A3.E15" title="Equation C.15 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.15</span></a>). This function
belongs to <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(q_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(q_{y})</annotation></semantics></math> and has <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>-mean zero; since the
subtracted affine function is <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>-centered, <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> has
<math id="A3.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>-mean zero as well.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The coefficient <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen to center the gradient
of <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>: differentiating the preceding identity and averaging
under <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\nabla_{u}(\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w)(u)\,q_{y}(\mathrm{d}u)=2\sqrt{\eta}\,\mathbb{E}[\nabla w(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]=2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\nabla_{u}(\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w)(u)\,q_{y}(\mathrm{d}u)=2\sqrt{\eta}\,\mathbb{E}[\nabla w(Y_{-})\mid Y_{+}=y]=2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">and hence</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{u}e_{y}(W)=2\sqrt{\eta}\,\{\nabla w(Y_{-})-a_{y}\}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{u}e_{y}(W)=2\sqrt{\eta}\,\{\nabla w(Y_{-})-a_{y}\}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> has Poincaré constant at most <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[e_{y}(W)^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\leq\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla_{u}e_{y}(W)\|^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]=4\eta\,\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla w(Y_{-})-a_{y}\|^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[e_{y}(W)^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\leq\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla_{u}e_{y}(W)\|^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]=4\eta\,\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla w(Y_{-})-a_{y}\|^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Integrating in <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and expanding the square using the definition of
<math id="A3.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> proves (<a href="#A3.E17" title="Equation C.17 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.17</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We turn to the energy estimate. We may assume <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that
<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{y}(u)=\sqrt{\eta}\,\nabla V(y+\sqrt{\eta}u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.317em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{y}(u)=\sqrt{\eta}\,\nabla V(y+\sqrt{\eta}u)</annotation></semantics></math>, so that
<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla V(X)=\eta^{-1/2}g_{y}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V(X)=\eta^{-1/2}g_{y}(W)</annotation></semantics></math>, and that
<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(W,g_{y}(W)\mid Y_{+}=y)=I-\Sigma_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(W,g_{y}(W)\mid Y_{+}=y)=I-\Sigma_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> by
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Conditional gradient covariance bound). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>. The decomposition
(<a href="#A3.E15" title="Equation C.15 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.15</span></a>) therefore gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(w(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)=2(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}+\eta^{-1/2}\varepsilon_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\varepsilon_{y}\coloneqq\mathrm{Cov}(e_{y}(W),g_{y}(W)\mid Y_{+}=y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(w(Y_{-}),\nabla V(X)\mid Y_{+}=y)=2(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}+\eta^{-1/2}\varepsilon_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\varepsilon_{y}\coloneqq\mathrm{Cov}(e_{y}(W),g_{y}(W)\mid Y_{+}=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this into (<a href="#A3.E8" title="Equation C.8 ‣ Lemma C.1 (Derivative formula for 𝖴_𝖯𝖯). ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w](y)=\nabla w(y)-a_{y}+2(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}+\eta^{-1/2}\varepsilon_{y}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w](y)=\nabla w(y)-a_{y}+2(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}+\eta^{-1/2}\varepsilon_{y}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Conditional Cauchy–Schwarz and
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Conditional gradient covariance bound). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a> give, for every
<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varepsilon_{y}^{\top}v|^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\,\mathbb{E}[e_{y}(W)^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\,v^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})v\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varepsilon_{y}^{\top}v|^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\,\mathbb{E}[e_{y}(W)^{2}\mid Y_{+}=y]\,v^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})v\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">We will also use</span></p>
<table id="A3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\preceq I-\Sigma_{y}\preceq\beta\eta I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\preceq I-\Sigma_{y}\preceq\beta\eta I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">The two-sided bound in
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, together with the fact that
<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> fixes constants, gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})^{2}\preceq 3\,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})^{2}\preceq 3\,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">on <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="A3.SS3.p8.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{y}=(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\nabla w)(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{y}=(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\nabla w)(y)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> acting coordinatewise,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}=\bigl\langle\nabla w,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})\nabla w\bigr\rangle\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\int\|\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq 3\mathcal{R}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.000em">,</mo><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}=\bigl\langle\nabla w,(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})\nabla w\bigr\rangle\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\int\|\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq 3\mathcal{R}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now control <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and the affine energy simultaneously.
Take the <math id="A3.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> inner product of
(<a href="#A3.E19" title="Equation C.19 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.19</span></a>) with the vector field
<math id="A3.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\mapsto\nabla w(y)+a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\mapsto\nabla w(y)+a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)=\mathcal{R}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)=\mathcal{R}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain the exact identity</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}+4\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}+4\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int[\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w](y)^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int[\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w](y)^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt-2\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt-2\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt-\eta^{-1/2}\int\varepsilon_{y}^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt-\eta^{-1/2}\int\varepsilon_{y}^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We bound the three terms on the right separately. For the first,
conditional Jensen gives <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\|a_{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq\|\nabla w\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\|a_{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq\|\nabla w\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and hence</span></p>
<table id="A3.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Bigl\lvert\int[\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w](y)^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\rvert\leq 2\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.039em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.039em">∥</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl\lvert\int[\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w](y)^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\rvert\leq 2\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the second, Cauchy–Schwarz,
(<a href="#A3.E21" title="Equation C.21 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.21</span></a>), and
(<a href="#A3.E22" title="Equation C.22 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.22</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\,\Bigl|\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr|\leq C\sqrt{\beta\eta}\,\mathcal{R}^{1/2}\,\Bigl\{\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\,\Bigl|\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr|\leq C\sqrt{\beta\eta}\,\mathcal{R}^{1/2}\,\Bigl\{\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, using the pointwise identity
<math id="A3.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla w(y)+a_{y}=\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}+2a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla w(y)+a_{y}=\{\nabla w(y)-a_{y}\}+2a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#A3.E21" title="Equation C.21 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.21</span></a>) and
(<a href="#A3.E22" title="Equation C.22 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.22</span></a>) imply</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq C\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}+8\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\leq C\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}+8\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using (<a href="#A3.E20" title="Equation C.20 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.20</span></a>), Cauchy–Schwarz in <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#A3.E17" title="Equation C.17 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.17</span></a>), and
(<a href="#A3.E26" title="Equation C.26 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.26</span></a>), we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\eta^{-1/2}\,\Bigl|\int\varepsilon_{y}^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" lspace="0.150em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta^{-1/2}\,\Bigl|\int\varepsilon_{y}^{\top}\{\nabla w(y)+a_{y}\}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt\leq C\sqrt{\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}}\,\Bigl\{\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}+\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt\leq C\sqrt{\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}}\,\Bigl\{\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}+\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt\leq C\sqrt{\beta\eta}\,\mathcal{R}^{1/2}\,\Bigl\{\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}+C\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt\leq C\sqrt{\beta\eta}\,\mathcal{R}^{1/2}\,\Bigl\{\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}+C\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these three estimates into
(<a href="#A3.E23" title="Equation C.23 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.23</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}+4\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}+4\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex66.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.039em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt+C\sqrt{\beta\eta}\,\mathcal{R}^{1/2}\Bigl\{\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}+C\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt+C\sqrt{\beta\eta}\,\mathcal{R}^{1/2}\Bigl\{\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\Bigr\}^{1/2}+C\beta\eta\,\mathcal{R}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">For sufficiently small universal <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, the last two terms
are absorbed into the left-hand side. This proves (<a href="#A3.E18" title="Equation C.18 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.18</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition C.5 (Interpolation bound on the 𝖴_𝖯𝖯-spectral subspace associated with [1/2,1]). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choose a small enough universal constant in the hypothesis, if necessary, so
that <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a> applies. On
<math id="A3.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[1/2,1]}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ran</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{ran}(\mathbf{1}_{[1/2,1]}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}))</annotation></semantics></math>, the operator
<math id="A3.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded.
Applying (<a href="#A2.E13" title="Equation B.13 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.13</span></a>) first to
<math id="A3.SS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}w</annotation></semantics></math> and then to
<math id="A3.SS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{\eta}\,\|\nabla w\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{\eta}\,\|\nabla w\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}w\|\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}w\|\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}w\|\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}w\|\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{\eta}\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{\eta}\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{3}w\|\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{-1}(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\leq C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{3}w\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here, the final inequality in each line follows by spectral calculus
on <math id="A3.SS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\frac{1}{2},1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\frac{1}{2},1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Decompose <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w</annotation></semantics></math> according to
(<a href="#A3.E15" title="Equation C.15 ‣ Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.15</span></a>). The affine part has
coefficient <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\sqrt{\eta}\,a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition C.2 (Weighted half-turn estimate for affine functions). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\|\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\|\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>
applied to the error term, and <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r+s)^{2}\leq 2r^{2}+2s^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r+s)^{2}\leq 2r^{2}+2s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> give</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\beta\eta^{2}\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)+C\,\mathbb{E}[e_{Y_{+}}(W)^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\beta\eta^{2}\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)+C\,\mathbb{E}[e_{Y_{+}}(W)^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\eta\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.039em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.317em">∥</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\eta\,\|\nabla(I-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}})w\|\,\|\nabla w\|\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last line uses <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma C.6 (Conditional affine approximation and energy bound). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>. Finally,
(<a href="#A3.E28" title="Equation C.28 ‣ Proof of . ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.28</span></a>) gives (<a href="#A3.E14" title="Equation C.14 ‣ Proposition C.5 (Interpolation bound on the 𝖴_𝖯𝖯-spectral subspace associated with [1/2,1]). ‣ C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.14</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
